    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1120">

                <pb facs="0932" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.111 Ad 11.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-05T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 5, 1912—8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following to American Consuls at Ciudad Juárez and Chihuahua:</p>
                <p>[See next above.]</p>
                <p>Make immediate urgent representations to the Mexican Government regarding
                    absolute necessity of protection of American life and property by that
                    Government to the utmost of its power.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
